# Testing Conventions

## Backend Tests (pytest)

### Integration Tests (`backend/tests/integration_tests/`)

- Marker: `@pytest.mark.asyncio(loop_scope="session")`
- Fixtures: `reinit_database` (session), `auth_context` (session), `startup_and_shutdown_uvicorn_server` (module)
- Helpers: `send_auth_request()`, `send_tournament_request()`, `send_request()`
- HTTP methods: use `HTTPMethod` enum, not raw strings
- Assert full JSON payloads including `data` wrapper
- Test data: `inserted_*` async context managers, `DUMMY_*` records
- DB: real PostgreSQL on port 5532 (CI service)

### Unit Tests (`backend/tests/unit_tests/`)

- No HTTP server — construct Pydantic models directly
- Use `DUMMY_*` fixtures and negative IDs for isolation
- `test_openapi_up_to_date` enforces spec freshness

### Running

```bash
cd backend
ENVIRONMENT=CI uv run pytest --cov .   # full suite
uv run pytest tests/unit_tests/        # unit only
```

## Frontend Tests

No runtime/component tests. `pnpm test` runs:
- `tsc` (type checking)
- `prettier --write` (formatting)

## CI Quality Gates

### Backend (`backend.yml`)
- pytest + coverage → Codecov
- mypy, pyrefly (type checkers)
- pylint, ruff format, ruff check (linting)
- vulture (dead code — flags unused functions/classes/methods)

### Frontend (`frontend.yml`)
- `pnpm test` = tsc + prettier (no eslint in CI despite config existing)

### Docker (`docker-build.yml`)
- Builds all 3 Dockerfiles on PRs (no push)

### Pre-commit (local)
- `cd backend && ./precommit.sh` runs the full backend quality suite
